Description: Tell once when the monitor cannot show a 3D video in 3D
 With Preview at 3D, a 3D area that could not be made (the window had no Wayland
 surface, the declaration library could not start, the compositor did not take
 stereo content) left the monitor transparent with nothing said, and a refused
 declaration was a log line while the views were shown side by side flat. Now the
 layer says why (StereoLayer::failed), the monitor tells the person once in its
 own message area and shows the packed frame as it is, and tries 3D again when the
 person chooses a preview. On X11 under a compositor that takes stereo content
 (stereo_supported_x11), where the 3D area, a Wayland surface, cannot be made, the
 monitor says once that it shows 3D only when Kdenlive runs on Wayland. On a
 desktop that takes no stereo content nothing is said: the menu has no 3D entry.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-20

--- a/src/monitor/monitor.cpp
+++ b/src/monitor/monitor.cpp
